  "answer": "Fixed. The backend's delete endpoint is `DELETE /api/v1/cart/{code}/product/{sku}`, and its facade matches the line item with `shoppingCartItem.getProduct().getSku().equals(sku)` \u2014 if nothing matches, it just returns an unchanged cart with a 204, which is exactly why \"removing\" an item silently did nothing.\n\nThe frontend was building the URL with `item.id` (the numeric product ID), which never equals the product's SKU, so the backend found no item to delete. The fix changes line 163 of [cartActions.js](~/code/benchmark/okf-local/main/source/work/g1_delete_item/source/codex/4/src/redux/actions/cartActions.js:163) to send `item.sku` instead \u2014 the same field `addToCart` already uses as the product identifier.\n\nFiles used:\n- `src/redux/actions/cartActions.js` (fixed, only file changed)\n- `src/util/constant.js` and `src/util/webService.js` (to confirm the request path)\n- `src/pages/other/Cart.js` (confirmed the whole cart item object is passed in)\n- Backend: `BasketEndpoint.java` (route/contract) and `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` (SKU matching logic) in `~/code/benchmark/okf-local/pr2`",
